Track 2: Who Poured Salt in the Loran-C?
- Story & Context: Huddled in the damp basalt foundation of the Spitsbergen Sound lighthouse with the metallic, chemical taste of canned condensed milk lingering on her tongue, Clara do Mar wept openly into her maritime headset during an unscheduled two-hour pirated transmission. Her fingers were so numb that she could no longer form minor-seventh chords on her nylon guitar, forcing her to lean on the drone of a freezing Juno-60 while the 808's booming sub-bass thudded rhythmically through the salt-crusted floorboards. Cod trawlers traversing the zero-visibility blizzard listened in total silence as she confessed into the open channel that she had sabotaged the station’s radio navigation unit with brine just to buy more time alone before the spring relief cutter arrived: "Forgive my fingers on the fader, the ice has no chorus." By dawn, three separate ship captains refused to report her coordinates to the maritime police, choosing instead to drift silently in the swell so they wouldn't lose her signal.
